{"judgments": [
  {"clause_id": "c001", "issues": [
    {"issue": "This face-page promise is to pay \"the Death Benefit\" in a lump sum, but Section 6 (Death Proceeds) makes the amount actually payable the Death Benefit plus rider insurance less any Policy Debt. A beneficiary could argue the cover-page promise controls the amount payable at death.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.30}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c002", "issues": []},
  {"clause_id": "c003", "issues": [
    {"issue": "\"Replacements,\" which triggers the 60-day rather than 10-day return window, is nowhere defined in the policy. The provision also promises a refund of premium while simultaneously deducting withdrawals and loans from a policy declared \"void from its beginning.\"", "type": 1, "prob": 0.16}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c004", "issues": [
    {"issue": "The Schedule states \"Additional Ratings Not Applicable\" while the same page classifies the Insured as \"Percentage Substandard 150.0%\" and the Policy Acceptance Form amendment states \"Base policy is rated.\" Which of these governs the rating charge under Section 9(d) is open to construction.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.24}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c005", "issues": [
    {"issue": "This notice conditions continuation on \"the Net Policy Value, less Policy Debt,\" but Section 3 defines Net Policy Value as already being Policy Value less Policy Debt, so debt is deducted twice. Section 11's Grace Period test uses Net Policy Value alone.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.30}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c006", "issues": [
    {"issue": "This notice states the policy \"will not lapse at any time\" before the end of the Guaranteed Death Benefit Period if the Total Cumulative Premium Test is met, but Section 11 provides that the policy goes into default whenever Policy Debt exceeds Policy Value, with no carve-out for that period. The two cannot both be given full effect.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.26}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c007", "issues": []},
  {"clause_id": "c008", "issues": [
    {"issue": "The Surrender Charge note says the charges \"will reduce on a monthly basis to equal zero over time, as shown in this table,\" while the table shows only annual amounts as of the beginning of each Policy Year. The rate and method of the monthly reduction between Policy Years is left unstated.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.22}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c009", "issues": [
    {"issue": "The Rider Information line shows a Benefit Amount of \"None\" and no rider charge for the Living Benefit Rider, while the rider itself specifies a Maximum Accelerated Benefit of $250,000. Whether the Schedule Page or the rider fixes the benefit is contestable.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.22}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c010", "issues": [
    {"issue": "The Table of Values sets a \"Maximum Annual Premium\" of $1,000,000 while the same table sets a Guideline Single Premium of $4,195,289.66 that Section 4 permits to be paid, and Section 4 forbids refusing any premium needed to prevent termination. Which limit governs a large single payment is unresolved.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.24}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c011", "issues": [
    {"issue": "This footnote asserts an unqualified right to \"change ... the amount of cost of insurance deducted,\" whereas Section 9 permits re-determination only on a basis that does not discriminate unfairly within a class and forbids recouping prior losses. A policyholder challenging a rate increase would say the two cannot be read together.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.35}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c012", "issues": [
    {"issue": "This notice flatly promises Additional Interest on amounts above the Policy Value Benchmark Amount, but the Section 9 table sets the Additional Interest Rate at 0% whenever the credited rate is under 4.25%, and the Guaranteed Minimum Interest Rate is only 4%. Read with Section 9 the promised credit may never arise.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.24}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c013", "issues": []},
  {"clause_id": "c014", "issues": [
    {"issue": "The unisex Monthly Factor is stated as \"4.0032737\" where the sex-distinct factor in the same table is 1.0032737, an evident transcription error that would quadruple the divisor used in the Net Amount at Risk calculation. The correct figure must be supplied by construction.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.26}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c015", "issues": []},
  {"clause_id": "c016", "issues": []},
  {"clause_id": "c017", "issues": [
    {"issue": "\"Attained Age\" is defined as \"the Age plus the number of whole years that have elapsed since the Policy Date,\" but \"Age\" is itself defined as the person's age on the given date, so the elapsed years are counted twice. This drives the Age 100 Anniversary, the Maturity Date and the Minimum Death Benefit Percentages.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.28}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c018", "issues": [
    {"issue": "\"Business day\" is defined as \"any day that we are open for business,\" a term whose content is fixed unilaterally by the insurer and has no calendar boundary. Values under Sections 9, 15 and 25 turn on it.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.12}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c019", "issues": [
    {"issue": "After enumerating a death certificate and a court order, the definition adds the catch-all \"any other proof acceptable to us,\" leaving the sufficiency of proof to the insurer's judgment. Whether the catch-all is limited by the enumerated specifics is a classic ejusdem generis question.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.24}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c020", "issues": [
    {"issue": "\"In force\" is defined by reference to the Grace Period provision, but Section 11 contemplates a policy \"in default\" yet still within a 61-day grace period, and Section 6 pays proceeds for a death during that period. Whether a defaulted policy is \"in force\" for purposes of Sections 6, 14 and 15 is unsettled.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.22}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c021", "issues": [
    {"issue": "A writing counts only if \"satisfactory to us,\" and the definition extends to \"such other medium electronic or otherwise that we may from time to time make available,\" neither of which has a fixed standard. Every owner election in the policy depends on this term.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.16}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c022", "issues": [
    {"issue": "\"Issue Date\" is defined only by the effect it has (the date from which Suicide Exclusion and Incontestability run) and not by any event, so the definition is circular. It gives no rule for fixing the date if the Schedule Page entry were disputed.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.15}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c023", "issues": [
    {"issue": "The \"Maturity Date\" is defined as the date the Insured reaches Attained Age 100, yet Section 8 expressly provides for coverage, credited interest and death benefits continuing after the Age 100 Anniversary. Whether the policy matures and ends on that date, or continues, is left open.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.28}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c024", "issues": []},
  {"clause_id": "c025", "issues": []},
  {"clause_id": "c026", "issues": []},
  {"clause_id": "c027", "issues": []},
  {"clause_id": "c028", "issues": []},
  {"clause_id": "c029", "issues": [
    {"issue": "The definition ends \"that you intend to be pay on a regular modal basis,\" an ungrammatical and unpunctuated clause. The garble leaves unclear whether the Planned Premium is an obligation or a mere intention.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.11}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c030", "issues": []},
  {"clause_id": "c031", "issues": []},
  {"clause_id": "c032", "issues": []},
  {"clause_id": "c033", "issues": []},
  {"clause_id": "c034", "issues": [
    {"issue": "This definition computes Policy Value by daily accumulation with interest, while Section 9 credits interest only on each Monthly Calculation Date and adds Additional Interest on the same monthly cycle. The two accumulation mechanics are not obviously reconcilable.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.20}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c035", "issues": []},
  {"clause_id": "c036", "issues": [
    {"issue": "The \"Preferred Loan\" definition presupposes a loan carried over from a previously issued policy, but Section 1 shows a Preferred Loan Amount at Issue of $0, so the defined category may have no application here. Section 1's Preferred Policy Loan Interest Rate and credited rate nonetheless assume it exists.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.12}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c037", "issues": [
    {"issue": "The definition of \"Surrender Value\" is truncated in the instrument (\"and less ~any-unpaid.issue. charges a\"), leaving the final deduction incompletely stated. Net Surrender Value, the Grace Period test after year 9 and the surrender payment all depend on it.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.22}
